<rml>
<head>
    <title>Settings</title>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="tokens.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="case.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="mark.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="window.rcss"/>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="scrim" id="settings-scrim">
        <div class="case">

            <div class="lid stacked">
                <div class="lid-top">
                    <div class="head">
                        <div class="mark"></div>
                        <div class="title">Settings</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="chrome">
                        <div class="win-btn" id="modal-close"><div class="glyph-x"><div class="bar a"></div><div class="bar b"></div></div></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="hint">Up and down to move, left and right to change, Escape or the pad's B closes</div>
            </div>

            <!-- THE ROWS ARE BUILT FROM THE MODEL, NOT LISTED HERE, exactly as the controls
                 document and the debug menu build theirs. This used to be a fixed run of row
                 elements, and on 2026-09-22 adding two settings pushed three rows off the end of
                 it: a row with no element simply does not appear, so Controls, Your files and
                 Debug vanished while the menu looked perfectly normal. Slots were added, and then
                 the user asked the better question ("but can we not just add scrollable areas?"),
                 which is this. There is now no number here to get wrong, and a list longer than
                 the case scrolls instead of being cut off. -->
            <div class="rows long" id="settings-rows"></div>

            <!-- Quit is an ACTION, drawn in the same bar the launcher uses, alone: there is
                 nothing to Play from inside the game. It was missing here altogether once the two
                 buttons left the list (the user, 2026-09-23), and with the title bar off this
                 menu is the only way out of the program. It keeps its place at the end of the
                 keyboard and pad order. -->
            <div class="actions">
                <div class="act-btn act-quit" id="act-quit"><span class="act-label" id="act-quit-label">Quit</span></div>
            </div>

            <div class="foot">
                <span>Saved as you change it</span>
                <span id="settings-foot">F1 closes this, F2 is about, F3 is controls</span>
            </div>

        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
